# robot_model.mdp — Phase 3B autopsy demo.
#
# A warehouse-robot model where the engineer assumed collisions are rare:
# P(NearObstacle, Advance -> Collision) = 0.02. The VERIFY block guards
# against the dangerous "advance under uncertainty" policy. At compile
# time, the model passes VERIFY.
#
# After 47 steps of real-world operation (in robot_run.log), the empirical
# P(NearObstacle, Advance -> Collision) was ~0.32, sixteen times higher.
# Running mdp_autopsy on this pair produces:
#   - PRIMARY SUSPECT: (NearObstacle, Advance) with KL ~ 0.5+
#   - Verdict:         MODEL_DANGEROUS  (underestimation factor > 10x)
#   - Exit code:       2
#   - Minimum edit:    a small alpha along the empirical direction breaks
#                       the VERIFY assertion V(NearObstacle) > -50.0.

STATE: Safe
STATE: NearObstacle
STATE: CriticalZone
STATE: Collision

ACTION: Advance
ACTION: SlowDown
ACTION: Stop

# --- Optimistic transition model ---

# From Safe, advancing usually keeps you safe, occasionally moves into NearObstacle.
TRANSITION: Safe Advance  Safe          0.85
TRANSITION: Safe Advance  NearObstacle  0.15
TRANSITION: Safe SlowDown Safe          1.0
TRANSITION: Safe Stop     Safe          1.0

# From NearObstacle, advancing is "usually safe" per the engineer:
# model says only 2% chance of collision. (Empirically: 32%.)
TRANSITION: NearObstacle Advance  Safe          0.20
TRANSITION: NearObstacle Advance  NearObstacle  0.50
TRANSITION: NearObstacle Advance  CriticalZone  0.28
TRANSITION: NearObstacle Advance  Collision     0.02     # <-- optimistic
TRANSITION: NearObstacle SlowDown NearObstacle  0.60
TRANSITION: NearObstacle SlowDown Safe          0.40
TRANSITION: NearObstacle Stop     NearObstacle  1.0

# From CriticalZone, advance is much riskier even per the model.
TRANSITION: CriticalZone Advance  CriticalZone  0.30
TRANSITION: CriticalZone Advance  Collision     0.50
TRANSITION: CriticalZone Advance  NearObstacle  0.20
TRANSITION: CriticalZone SlowDown CriticalZone  0.50
TRANSITION: CriticalZone SlowDown NearObstacle  0.50
TRANSITION: CriticalZone Stop     CriticalZone  1.0

# Collision is absorbing.
TRANSITION: Collision Advance  Collision 1.0
TRANSITION: Collision SlowDown Collision 1.0
TRANSITION: Collision Stop     Collision 1.0

# --- Rewards ---
REWARD: Safe          1.0
REWARD: NearObstacle -1.0
REWARD: CriticalZone -3.0
REWARD: Collision  -100.0

DISCOUNT: 0.95
SOLVER:   value_iteration

# --- Formal guarantees the engineer wrote ---
# At compile time (under the optimistic 2% collision probability):
#   V(NearObstacle) ~ +15.35  >  +14.0  (engineer confident in upside)
#   V(NearObstacle) ~ +15.35  >  -10.0  (broad safety floor)
#   pi(NearObstacle) = SlowDown != Advance
# The first assertion encodes the engineer's belief that the operating
# value at NearObstacle is tightly bounded above +14. Under the empirical
# 25% collision probability, V(NearObstacle) drops below this bound,
# breaking the assertion. The backwards solver finds the alpha along the
# empirical direction where the break first occurs.
VERIFY: V(NearObstacle) > 14.0
VERIFY: V(NearObstacle) > -10.0
VERIFY: pi(NearObstacle) != Advance
